<title>POLAND: VW increases stake in Polish unit.</title>
<headline>VW increases stake in Polish unit.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Volkswagen AG has increased its stake in its small Polish subisidiary by buying shares from the Polish Development Bank (PBR), the bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that PBR sold Volkswagen more than 1.5 million shares in the venture, called  Volkswagen Poznan Sp. z o.o. and based near the western city of Poznan, for more than six million marks.</p>
<p>As a result Volkswagen's stake in the company increased to 87.8 percent from 71.9 percent.</p>
<p>A Volkswagen official, who asked not to be named, told Reuters the purchase was connected to the German firm's expansion plans in Poland.</p>
<p>Volkswagen assembles Czech-made Skoda cars in the plant.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
